invariant: INV-26
file: aes_block.h
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: aes_block.h stops refusing CH_AES_HW and CH_AES_RUNTIME, the
  defines that chose the AES instructions when the object was built. A
  tree with its own build system that still writes one then compiles the
  AES=soft table under it, with no error, and believes it holds the
  instructions (docs/decisions.md 89). quic-builds.sh compiles aes_block.h
  under each define and requires the refusal.

--- old
#if defined(CH_AES_HW) || defined(CH_AES_RUNTIME)
#error "AES=hw and AES=runtime are gone: a host object holds the AES instructions (decision 89)"
#endif
--- new
